(a) Except as provided below, no alcoholic beverages shall be sold for consumption, stored for on-premises consumption, or otherwise consumed by customers, invitees, or the public on the premises of a commercial business.
(1) The following licensed establishments, locations, or businesses, as defined in this article, may be authorized to sell or provide customers with alcoholic beverages provided that the use is permissible under the applicable zoning regulations and by section 4-39 of this article:
a. Eating establishments or restaurants;
b. Brewpubs;
c. Bars;
d. Microbreweries or craft breweries;
e. Distilleries;
f. Event halls provided that the event hall is licensed to sell or provide alcoholic beverages and such beverages are sold, distributed, or otherwise provided through the event hall's employees holding a valid permit or such beverages are sold or provided through a caterer licensed in accordance with section 4-59;
g. Wine specialty shops; or
h. The location of a permitted catered event as defined in section 4-59.
(b) Any eating establishment or restaurant, as defined in this article, where alcoholic beverages are sold for consumption on the premises shall have a seating capacity of at least 75 persons excluding stools and counters.
(c) The only advertisement or sign indicating that alcoholic beverages may be consumed on the premises shall be a menu stating the name, brand or type of alcoholic beverages served and the price per serving. No other sign may be displayed either within or without the eating establishment indicating that alcoholic beverages are sold or may be consumed on the premises.
(d) On or before the 20th day of the month following the end of each calendar quarter, the licensee shall file with the Finance and Administrative Services Department a gross income report for the proceeding calendar quarter certified under oath by the licensee, which contains a percentage breakdown of the amount of alcoholic beverage sales relative to the establishment's total gross income from the sale of prepared meals and food for the preceding applicable quarter. Failure to file a timely and complete report as provided herein, or the filing of an incomplete or fraudulent report, shall constitute grounds for the suspension or revocation of the license issued by the city to such licensee.
(Code 1979, § 9-4-22; Code 1998, § 6-49; Ord. No. 17-2000, 12-4-2000; Ord. No. 07-2003, § 6-49, 7-7-2003; Ord. No. 05-2018, § 1, 5-7-2018; Ord. No. 04-2021, § I, 4-5-2021; Ord. No. 07-2021, § I, 7-6-2021; Ord. No. 07-2022, § I, 8-1-2022; Ord. No. 05-2023, § I, 7-10-2023)

